From e320c929207aaea0d4c8fb2cd29b16de6cbd2b2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michal Klocek <michal.klocek@qt.io>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 16:41:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] CMake: Improve qt config override handling

Make find_package calls not throwing errors from override handling. We
should print just the warning and let the find_package call itself to
'throw' the error when required. (namely when REQUIRED is set as
argument and returned version is not fine.) Simplify override handling
and use override only when version being asked is greater then qt build
version, as this the case when we require overriding.

In case override files are inconsistent or not provided simply return qt
config version. Make sure if we bail out we load base file.

Task-number: QTBUG-150218
Change-Id: I4cdc46399639a088b18b8656edde5ab2804ca039
Reviewed-by: Alexandru Croitor <alexandru.croitor@qt.io>
(cherry picked from commit f6bdd926180b0f24f0ce0b270b498483980018f0)
Reviewed-by: Jani Heikkinen <jani.heikkinen@qt.io>
